%N A397822 a(n) = round(j(sqrt(-n))), where j is j-invariant.
%C A397822 a(n) is close to exp(2*Pi*sqrt(n)) + 744, since j(tau) = 1/q + 744 + 196884*q + ... with q = exp(2*Pi*i*tau) = exp(-2*Pi*sqrt(n)) here.
%e A397822    n |    j(sqrt(-n))   |    a(n)
%e A397822   ---+------------------+-----------
%e A397822    1 |      1728        |      1728
%e A397822    2 |      8000        |      8000
%e A397822    3 |     54000        |     54000
%e A397822    4 |    287496        |    287496
%e A397822    5 |   1264538.909... |   1264539
%e A397822    6 |   4831907.903... |   4831908
%e A397822    7 |  16581375        |  16581375
%e A397822    8 |  52249767.137... |  52249767
%e A397822    9 | 153553679.396... | 153553679
%e A397822   10 | 425671414.618... | 425671415
%o A397822 (PARI) a(n) = round(ellj(sqrt(n)*I));
